# ripgrep / fd ignore rules (higher precedence than .gitignore).
#
# .gitignore hides sources/ from git on purpose. That also hid it from
# root-level ripgrep, so cross-component search silently returned nothing.
#
# Whitelist the component directories only -- NOT their contents. An .ignore
# whitelist outranks .gitignore at any depth, so `!/sources/**` would switch
# off every component's own .gitignore and flood results with node_modules,
# .venv and build output. Stopping the whitelist at the directory lets each
# component's .gitignore govern its own subtree, exactly as it does when you
# run ripgrep from inside that repo.
!/sources/*/

# Ripgrep skips dot-directories by default. Re-include the ones that hold
# tracked configuration worth searching across components.
!/sources/*/.github/
!/sources/*/.krci-ai/
!/sources/*/.chglog/

# Verify this file after adding a component; both sides should agree:
#   diff <(rg --files sources | sed 's|^sources/||' | sort) \
#        <(for r in sources/*/; do git -C "$r" ls-files -co --exclude-standard \
#            | sed "s|^|$(basename "$r")/|"; done | sort)
